<h1>array search</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Find an element in an <a href="array.html"><em>array</em></a>.  Various algorithms exist which require more or less structure in the array elements or implementation.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="linearSearch.html"><em>linear search</em></a>, <a href="binarySearch.html"><em>binary search</em></a>, <a href="interpolationSearch.html"><em>interpolation search</em></a>, <a href="stringMatching.html"><em>string matching</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
An <a href="externalindx.html"><em>external index</em></a>, such as a <a href="hashtab.html"><em>hash table</em></a> or <a href="invertedIndex.html"><em>inverted index</em></a> may help make the search quicker and speed overall processing if the array is not changed often.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPR">PR</a></p>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

